{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1788285389138,"sessionID":"ses_fa1e30e50ffeU2O2jnEUGTDEg1","part":{"id":"prt_05e1d894f001Lx72SI3EREj6ZF","messageID":"msg_05e1d83570014Q5YwWbP6RwD5E","sessionID":"ses_fa1e30e50ffeU2O2jnEUGTDEg1","snapshot":"f3635e20aefb1af17552c02c447060a0900efddc","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1788285403539,"sessionID":"ses_fa1e30e50ffeU2O2jnEUGTDEg1","part":{"id":"prt_05e1dbb7b001FcGBkCLH3YNiSu","messageID":"msg_05e1d83570014Q5YwWbP6RwD5E","sessionID":"ses_fa1e30e50ffeU2O2jnEUGTDEg1","type":"text","text":"The uncommitted work is genuine progress on this task. Let me preserve it via stash, then reset the branch to origin/main (which drops d9896ec and the stale ESCALATION.md).\n\n","time":{"start":1788285401980,"end":1788285403536}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788285403560,"sessionID":"ses_fa1e30e50ffeU2O2jnEUGTDEg1","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b24ee32a77bb3e01","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git stash push -u -m \"offload explain WIP (gh:168)\""},"output":"Saved working directory and index state On issue-168: offload explain WIP (gh:168)\n","metadata":{"output":"Saved working directory and index state On issue-168: offload explain WIP (gh:168)\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git stash push -u -m \"offload explain WIP (gh:168)\"","time":{"start":1788285403550,"end":1788285403557}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Good. The uncommitted work is real progress on this lane. Now I need to:\n1. Stash the uncommitted work (including untracked src/offload.rs and scratch_off.toy).\n2. Reset --hard to origin/main (drops d9896ec and ESCALATION.md).\n3. Pop the stash.\n\nBut wait - there's a subtlety. The uncommitted work references things like `tir::{Kind, Program, Tir}`, `Type`, `contains_vec`, `as_opt`. These may or may not exist on origin/main. Since the reset drops d9896ec, but the working tree changes were made against d9896ec's version of the code. If origin/main is a superset (d9896ec not ancestor but... hmm d9896ec is NOT an ancestor). \n\nWait, this is confusing. d9896ec is NOT an ancestor of origin/main, yet the brief says gh:162's research \"already landed on main via issue-166 (a678620)\". So origin/main contains equivalent content via a different commit (a678620 = issue-166, \"per-file definition origin + visibility, module-routing spike\"). So origin/main's module-routing is equivalent, just different commit.\n\nSo the uncommitted work in src/offload.rs, lib.rs, main.rs was written against d9896ec's tree. When I pop the stash after resetting to origin/main, there could be conflicts if origin/main changed src/lib.rs or src/main.rs. But git stash pop will apply cleanly if the context matches, or may conflict. Since the changes are only additions (adding offload module, adding a flag), likely applies fine.\n\nActually, a cleaner approach given the constraints (no heredocs, no rm, one command per bash call): I could avoid stash entirely by using `git stash` and `git stash pop`. But stash is a git command, allowed? The denials list mentions rm, env-prefixed commands, loops, heredocs, file writes, /tmp, multi-command lines. git stash should be fine.\n\nLet me do: `git stash push -u` (include untracked), then `git reset --hard origin/main`, then `git stash pop`.\n\nActually, `git stash push -u -m \"offload WIP\"`. Then reset. Then pop.\n\nLet me be careful: the stash includes scratch_off.toy which I'll probably want to drop (it's a scratch file). But brief says scratch files I cannot delete are fine, just don't git add them. So I can keep it as untracked after pop and just not add it.\n\nActually let me reconsider. The brief says \"keep what applies after the reset, drop what doesn't.\" After reset + pop, I'll have the offload work. Then I'll verify it compiles against origin/main. If offload.rs references types that don't exist on main, I fix it. scratch_off.toy is a test input - probably keep for testing but don't commit.\n\nLet me do the stash and reset.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05e1dc039001Dwmqe0lq99N1H3","sessionID":"ses_fa1e30e50ffeU2O2jnEUGTDEg1","messageID":"msg_05e1d83570014Q5YwWbP6RwD5E"}}
