{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788285520007,"sessionID":"ses_fa1e30e50ffeU2O2jnEUGTDEg1","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a05e1f865778a39e3fe3ed","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"vectorizability|offload|kernel|admissible\" plans/questions.md | head -30"},"output":"28:| [Q8](#q8-is-vectorizability-visible-in-the-type-system-or-a-silent-optimization) | Is vectorizability visible in the type system, or a silent optimization? | OPEN |\n157:### Q8. Is vectorizability visible in the type system, or a silent optimization?\n245: kernel-admissibility result covers elementwise filters only, and this is the gap it leaves.\n249:Argued in [the admissible input set, and where batching comes from](../draft.md#the-admissible-input-set-and-where-batching-comes-from) rather than\n255:Argued in [the admissible input set, and where batching comes from](../draft.md#the-admissible-input-set-and-where-batching-comes-from), where it\n","metadata":{"output":"28:| [Q8](#q8-is-vectorizability-visible-in-the-type-system-or-a-silent-optimization) | Is vectorizability visible in the type system, or a silent optimization? | OPEN |\n157:### Q8. Is vectorizability visible in the type system, or a silent optimization?\n245: kernel-admissibility result covers elementwise filters only, and this is the gap it leaves.\n249:Argued in [the admissible input set, and where batching comes from](../draft.md#the-admissible-input-set-and-where-batching-comes-from) rather than\n255:Argued in [the admissible input set, and where batching comes from](../draft.md#the-admissible-input-set-and-where-batching-comes-from), where it\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"rg -n \"vectorizability|offload|kernel|admissible\" plans/questions.md | head -30","time":{"start":1788285520001,"end":1788285520005}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The flag works. The output annotates each sub-expression with its cardinality and whether it's an offloadable kernel or scalar fallback.\n\nNow let me think about the design more carefully. The issue says:\n\n\"Ruled in the multiplicity-and-offload-round2 grilling round (question vectorizability-visibility): silent, cardinality-derived vectorizability is confirmed, discoverable via an opt-in --explain-offload build flag that annotates compiled output with which sub-expressions became vectorized kernels and which fell back, and why. No type-system or signature change. Editor/LSP hover is a wanted future addition, deliberately unscheduled.\"\n\nSo the current implementation:\n1. Adds `--explain-offload` flag to main.rs\n2. Creates src/offload.rs with the `explain` function\n3. Annotates each sub-expression with cardinality and disposition\n\nLet me review the design against the round-2 ruling. Let me look at the referenced design docs: plans/questions.md Q8, draft.md \"Cardinality is the kernel-admissibility predicate\", \"The admissible input set\". Let me check these exist and what they say.\n\nWait - the brief says \"do not touch plans/\". But I can read them. Let me check the design docs to make sure the implementation matches the ruling.\n\nLet me look at the relevant designdocs.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05e1f86ca001Xcte531ZJLKdiy","sessionID":"ses_fa1e30e50ffeU2O2jnEUGTDEg1","messageID":"msg_05e1f5b8f001NchNw4dYQhPRDm"}}
