{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788285529064,"sessionID":"ses_fa1e30e50ffeU2O2jnEUGTDEg1","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a05e1fa5e97900ae1f916a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"Cardinality is the kernel-admissibility|admissible input set|offload\" draft.md | head -20"},"output":"803:## Backends, vectorization, and the offload boundary\n805:### Cardinality is the kernel-admissibility predicate\n818:So the offload boundary and the layer boundary are the same boundary. Everything in the value\n822:What still has to be excluded inside an offloaded region is the ordinary list: strings, objects,\n858:### The admissible input set, and where batching comes from\n1025:So the offload check and the \"will this vectorize\" check are nearly the same predicate. That is\n","metadata":{"output":"803:## Backends, vectorization, and the offload boundary\n805:### Cardinality is the kernel-admissibility predicate\n818:So the offload boundary and the layer boundary are the same boundary. Everything in the value\n822:What still has to be excluded inside an offloaded region is the ordinary list: strings, objects,\n858:### The admissible input set, and where batching comes from\n1025:So the offload check and the \"will this vectorize\" check are nearly the same predicate. That is\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"rg -n \"Cardinality is the kernel-admissibility|admissible input set|offload\" draft.md | head -20","time":{"start":1788285529059,"end":1788285529062}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me read the relevant draft.md sections: \"Cardinality is the kernel-admissibility predicate\" and \"The admissible input set\".","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05e1fa65d001hv0nAD4Wo6mJhJ","sessionID":"ses_fa1e30e50ffeU2O2jnEUGTDEg1","messageID":"msg_05e1f97e9001iRcHV7sbRbbQEZ"}}
